'''Villa Air''' is a Maldivian [[airline]]. It flies to only one destination, [[Maamigili (Alif Dhaalu Atoll)|Maamigili]], using four [[turboprop]] aircraft.<ref name="miadhu">{{Cite news |last=Latheef |first=Abdul |date=18 March 2011 |title=Villa introduces new airline 'Fly me” |url=http://www.miadhu.com/2011/03/local-news/villa-introduces-new-airline-%E2%80%98fly-me%E2%80%9D/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110322095654/http://www.miadhu.com/2011/03/local-news/villa-introduces-new-airline-%E2%80%98fly-me%E2%80%9D/ |archive-date=22 March 2011 |access-date=2011-03-17 |work=Miadhu}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=16 March 2011 |title=Villa “Fly Me” Brand Goes Airborne |url=http://www.haamadaily.com/englishdetails.php?news=21748 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110722005200/http://www.haamadaily.com/englishdetails.php?news=21748 |archive-date=22 July 2011 |access-date=2011-03-17 |work=Haama Daily}}</ref> Their headquarters are in the Villa House in [[Malé]].<ref name="flyme">{{cite web |title=Flyme - The Premier Domestic Airline of the Maldives, Maldivian Airline by Villa Air |url=http://www.flyme.mv |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171028041957/http://www.flyme.mv/ |archive-date=28 October 2017 |accessdate=2017-10-12 |website=flyme.mv}}</ref> The airline is a [[subsidiary]] of [[Villa Group]], and began operations on 1 October 2011.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Jameel |first=Abdullah |date=1 October 2011 |title=Maamigili airport opens with 'Flyme' airlines entering into service |url=http://www.haveeru.com.mv/news/37908 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111002070700/http://www.haveeru.com.mv/news/37908 |archive-date=2 October 2011 |access-date=2011-10-01 |work=[[Haveeru Daily]]}}</ref>  The company slogan is ''We fly you in style.''

==Destinations==
On 4 September 2020, the airline operated its first international charter flight from [[Velana International Airport]] to [[Bandaranaike International Airport]] carrying 72 passengers on an [[ATR 72-600]] aircraft.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nadalet |first=Ivan |date=7 September 2020 |title=Maldives' Flyme debuts international passenger operations |url=https://www.ch-aviation.com/portal/news/94936-maldives-flyme-debuts-international-passenger-operations |access-date=2023-08-16 |website=ch-aviation |language=en}}</ref>
 
